title the looking was the limit
prompt confirm BUHR is molted into stamp and name, silo it as a foundation, infuse it into a rota check -- plus the six-ship memory question
think Asked to confirm one ladder was molted, and built a meter rather than reading for it. The meter found five living forecasts where the question named one: SOON, JARL, BUHR, TACT, DISC, four equinoxes announcing 256 rungs between them against six reached.
think The meter's own two false-positive paths were caught by its control before it read the tree twice. An elder draft dropped the announced value from the reading, which made every FINISHED ladder read one rung short. A second draft named range spellings one by one and missed a Unicode ellipsis in a dated page, so one announcement voted a reach for another and SOON read as reaching SOON63.
think Fixed by requiring the separator to carry punctuation rather than enumerating spellings -- which keeps the script ASCII by law, since it cannot add the character to a list. The control proves that exact case with octal bytes.
think The rota seat was the right infusion. Earth-Cardinal read the one-clock spec, which names how a FILE is marked; the mark law extending it to WORK stood on no seat at all. The new foundation carries both halves for a first-day reader, and the spec and rule remain canonical one click away.
obs Answered the six-ship question by measuring rather than estimating. 8 GB and 4 vCPU, no swap; two live claudes hold 1.2 GB, load 1.71 with three ships berthed. Memory carries six comfortably. CPU carries about three: the roster is 904 CPU-seconds and six ships would spend 22 minutes a cycle on guards alone. Recommended two piers of three, with a falsifier that costs an afternoon and no money.
obs Both pins hit their ceilings this round. The card reached 69 bytes free before the landed accounts shelved; REDS went 967 bytes OVER before three closed rows folded. A pin at its ceiling taxes every lap, and both were carrying finished work.
obs Booked docs-geode for petrichor rather than taking it. The compressors are its lane and a claim is not a bypass.
